  "_comment": "Edge cases of a Yocto 6.x SPDX 3.0 image SBOM for parse-yocto-spdx.py. Licenses: a concluded NOASSERTION falling back to a real declared license (lic-fallback), declared NONE and CLOSED written as expressions (lic-none, lic-closed), a single LicenseRef (lic-ref). A purl with a percent-encoded version (libc6, as Yocto writes 2.44+git). One vulnerability linked from two recipes that judge it differently: fixed for liba, affected for libb. The image (primaryPurpose archive) also `generates` liba1 and has a vulnerability; only a specification package is a recipe, so neither its name nor its CVE reaches liba1. Expected parse: 7 components, licenses BSD-3-Clause / none / none / LicenseRef-Vendor-EULA (as a name); counts 1 fixed + 0 not-affected + 1 unresolved, the unresolved one on libb1.",
